00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:05.790
Here are two methods for decreasing
when knitting one by one ribbing.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:14.860
The simplest method is to just transfer the edge Stitch
to the opposite needle bed use your double eye

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.600
needle tool and remove the knit stitch from the
needle push the empty needle into out of work.

00:00:22.015 --> 00:00:29.115
Transfer that Stitch from the tool to the ribber needle
doubling up the stitches and knit two rows.

00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:41.175
Your next step is to slip the ribber Stitch to the double-wide
needle and transfer up to the main bed

00:00:41.365 --> 00:00:50.235
and double up the knit stitch knit two rows work
the decreases as instructed in your pattern.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.000
As many times as you need

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.240
the resulting Edge is smooth and clean

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.280
if you're going to seem to ribbed edges
you may want to use this method.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:19.580
There's more transferring of stitches, but you're
left with a seeming Stitch along the edge.

00:01:21.595 --> 00:01:29.695
Transfer the ribber Stitch to the main bed doubling
up the second Stitch from The Edge then transfer

00:01:29.695 --> 00:01:35.895
the edge knit stitch down to the ribber
this decreases one stitch.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:46.120
Again, transfer the main bed Stitch down to the second
ribber Stitch and move the edge ribber Stitch

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:49.780
to the main bed decreasing
another Stitch.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:57.860
Now keep in mind with this method The Edge Stitch will
always be a single stitch all the decreases.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:02.420
The doubled-up stitches are worked
on the Stitch next to the edge.

00:02:08.514 --> 00:02:15.185
As you can see the edge initially doesn't appear to be
as neat as the simple method but there's a stitch

00:02:15.185 --> 00:02:24.005
along the edge to make seeming easier the Knit It
Now learning library has many shaping technique

00:02:24.005 --> 00:02:30.105
tutorials for other needle Arrangements plus
tips and tricks for mastering your ribber.

00:02:31.555 --> 00:02:34.095
Thanks for watching and happy knitting.
